{"name":"Scampi","hex":"#6f63a0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scampi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Norway lobster, a langoustine (Nephrops norvegicus).\n The battered or breaded tails of this species, usually served with chips.","The battered or breaded tails of this species, usually served with chips."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of scampo"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scampi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scampi","blocks":[{"text":"Scampi is a crustacean-based seafood dish, typically featuring langoustine, prawns or shrimp sautéed in olive oil, garlic, and white wine, and garnished with Parmesan cheese and lemon juice, though exact ingredients vary regionally in preparation. The term \"scampi\" comes from the Italian name for langoustines, which were the original shellfish used in the dish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Nephrops_norvegicus.jpg/330px-Nephrops_norvegicus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scampi","wikidata":"Q10662375"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Scampi_served.jpg/500px-Scampi_served.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Scampi_served.jpg/500px-Scampi_served.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scampi served","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScampi_served.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Scampi_in_pikante_tomatensaus.jpg/500px-Scampi_in_pikante_tomatensaus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Scampi_in_pikante_tomatensaus.jpg/500px-Scampi_in_pikante_tomatensaus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut